# Agents Doctor (host-side)

## Purpose

Reconcile the agent system on disk against the central manifest
`.agents-system-setup/generated.json` and report drift. This is a host-side,
**read-only** check: it never edits files. Subagents never invoke it; the host
CLI session (or a human, or CI) runs it, reviews findings, and owns any fix or
migration decision.

The most important signal is a **stray `orchestrator` agent file**: the
orchestrator is the host CLI session reading `AGENTS.md`, never an emitted
subagent (no `orchestrator.agent.md` / `.claude/agents/orchestrator.md` /
`.opencode/agents/orchestrator.md` / `.codex/agents/orchestrator.toml` /
`.gemini/agents/orchestrator.md`). A generating session that hand-writes one
produces an unregistered file that no runtime resolves.

## How to run

Prefer the bundled engine; it is standard-library Python only and read-only:

```bash
python3 .agents-system-setup/agents-doctor.py          # human summary
python3 .agents-system-setup/agents-doctor.py --json    # machine-readable
python3 .agents-system-setup/agents-doctor.py --strict   # warnings fail (CI)
```

Exit codes: `0` clean · `1` error-severity findings (or warnings under
`--strict`) · `2` no manifest found.

If Python is unavailable, perform the same checks manually by reading the
manifest and scanning the runtime agent directories per the catalog below.

## Input contract

```yaml
root: <repo-root>            # default: parent of .agents-system-setup/
strict: false                # treat warnings as failures
```

The host does not expand the scan beyond the runtime agent directories
(`.github/agents`, `.claude/agents`, `.opencode/agents`, `.codex/agents`,
`.gemini/agents`), the skills paths, and `.agents-system-setup/`.

## Check catalog

| Signal | Severity | Detection rule |
|---|---|---|
| `orchestrator-subagent-file` | error | An agent file whose logical name is `orchestrator` exists in any runtime agents directory (always invalid per the host-session-is-orchestrator rule). |
| `stray-agent` | error | An agent file exists on disk but its path is absent from manifest `artifacts[]` (likely hand-written outside the plugin). |
| `missing-artifact` | error | A manifest `subagent` / `agents-md` artifact path is missing on disk. |
| `checksum-drift` | warn | A file's sha256 differs from the manifest `checksum` (edited since generation; content evolves naturally, so this is a warning). |
| `missing-stamp` | warn | An agent file has no `agents-system-setup:generated-by` stamp (pre-stamp or hand-authored). |
| `operational-state-artifact` | error | A forbidden subtree (`agents` / `skills` / `hooks` / `commands` / `prompts` / `plugins`) exists inside `.agents-system-setup/`. |
| `manifest-version-drift` | warn | The manifest `plugin_version` differs from the `AGENTS.md` stamp (suggest running upgrade mode). |

If `.agents-system-setup/generated.json` is absent, only
`orchestrator-subagent-file` and `operational-state-artifact` can run; the engine
exits `2` and the host should offer to (re-)run the plugin so a manifest exists.

## Output

The engine returns a findings list (`--json`):

```json
{
  "ok": false,
  "manifest_present": true,
  "counts": {"error": 1, "warn": 0},
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "error",
      "signal": "orchestrator-subagent-file",
      "path": ".github/agents/orchestrator.agent.md",
      "detail": "<why this is wrong>",
      "suggested_action": "<host-reviewed fix; never applied automatically>"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Reporting template

```text
Agents doctor: ok | findings
Manifest: <path | MISSING>
Errors: <count>  Warnings: <count>
Findings:
  - <severity> <signal> <path>: <detail> -> <suggested_action>
Handoff status: completed | blocked | returned-to-orchestrator
```

## Boundary rules (READ FIRST)

1. This skill is **READ-ONLY**. It returns findings and never modifies files.
2. This skill is **HOST-ONLY**. Subagents must not invoke it; if a subagent
   notices drift in its owned files it `return-to-orchestrator`.
3. Fixes are owned by the host orchestrator plus user approval. Stray/orchestrator
   removals go through the upgrade-mode migration ledger in
   `references/misplaced-artifacts-migration.md`, never a silent delete.
4. A clean result means no drift was found in the scanned surfaces only; it is
   not approval for any write.

## Anti-patterns

- Running this skill from inside a generated subagent.
- Auto-deleting a stray or orchestrator file because the finding looks obvious —
  route removals through the migration ledger with user approval.
- Treating `checksum-drift` as an error; content evolves and the warning is
  informational unless `--strict` is set for CI.
- Expanding the scan outside the runtime agent directories and
  `.agents-system-setup/`.
